--TEST--
A class constant whose value folds to nothing is refused where it is read and not where it is declared — `rule:classes/no-free-functions-or-constants`, `rule:attributes/payload-is-a-compile-time-constant`
--FILE--
<?nvs
// `rule:classes/no-free-functions-or-constants` inlines a class constant at every use site, so a declaration the
// constant folder cannot reduce to a value leaves a read with nothing to
// lower. Another class's constant folds only when its value is a number or a
// string, so one that is an array or an enum case has no constant form here.
enum Priority { Low, High }

final class Base {
    public const array<int> ONES = [1];
    public const Priority FIRST = Priority::Low;
}

final class Cfg {
    public const array<array<int>> NESTED = [Base::ONES];
    public const Priority START = Base::FIRST;
    // Declared and never read, which is legal: a constant nobody names costs
    // nothing and has no wrong behaviour to report, so the refusal is on the
    // read alone and this line contributes no diagnostic.
    public const array<array<int>> UNUSED = [Base::ONES];
}

echo Cfg::NESTED[0][0], "\n";
echo Cfg::START as int, "\n";
--EXPECT--

--EXPECTF-ERROR--
error[E0792]: `Cfg::NESTED` has no compile-time value to inline
   --> case.nvs:22:6
%A
error[E0792]: `Cfg::START` has no compile-time value to inline
   --> case.nvs:23:6
%A
error: aborting due to 2 errors
To read what a code means and how to fix it, run `nvs agent show <code>`.
